Why Linux Is Preferred Over Windows for Servers

1. Linux is Free (Open Source)

You don’t need to pay for licenses.

Companies can use thousands of servers without spending money on OS licenses.

Windows Server requires paid licenses.



---

2. Linux is Very Stable

Linux servers can run for years without needing a reboot.

It’s extremely reliable for long-running applications like websites, apps, databases.



---

3. Linux Uses Fewer Resources

It consumes less RAM and CPU.

You can run more applications on the same hardware.

Windows uses more memory and background services.



---

4. Strong Security

Linux is more secure by design:

Fewer viruses

Permission-based architecture

Quick security updates


Windows is often targeted more by malware.



---

5. Better for Developers

Linux supports:

Docker

Kubernetes

DevOps tools

Cloud-native apps

Servers like Apache, Nginx


It has built-in powerful CLI tools.



---

6. Control & Automation

Linux gives complete control over the OS.

You can automate everything using shell scripts.

Perfect for DevOps.



---

7. Popular in Cloud & Enterprises

AWS, Azure, GCP… most servers run on Linux.

Open-source ecosystem is huge.



---

8. Fast Updates and Customization

You can choose your distro (Ubuntu, CentOS, RHEL, Debian).

You can customize everything to your needs.

Windows has limited customization.



---

