RAM (64GB, 128GB, 512GB, etc.)

Storage (SSD, NVMe, RAID)

Network cards (1GbE, 10GbE, 40GbE)

Redundant power supply

Fans for cooling


Servers are built to handle heavy workloads.


---



---

3. Networking

Racks are connected with:

Switches

Routers

Firewalls


This gives data center servers 24/7 high-speed internet.




---

☁️ How Cloud Providers Use These Servers

AWS, Azure, GCP use these servers to create:

EC2 instances

Storage (S3)

Databases (RDS)

Load balancers


When you launch an server, you’re using one part of a physical server inside a rack.


---

