🖥️ What is a Hypervisor?

A hypervisor is a special software (or sometimes hardware layer) that allows you to run multiple virtual machines (VMs) on a single physical server.

Each VM behaves like its own independent computer.


---

🔍 Simple Example

You have one physical server → you want to run:

Windows Server

Linux Server

Ubuntu Desktop

RedHat Server


All on the same machine.

A hypervisor makes this possible.


---

🛠️ What Does the Hypervisor Do?

It divides the physical resources (CPU, RAM, storage, network) into parts and gives them to each VM.


🟢 In Short (Easy to Remember)

Hypervisor = Virtualization Software
Lets you create and run multiple virtual machines on one physical computer.
