A protocol is a set of rules that tells computers how to communicate with each other.

Think about it like human language and traffic rules.


“Ports” in computers are virtual doors that allow data to enter or leave a device (like a server, laptop, or mobile).
They help different applications communicate over a network.

Port is a logical communication Channel  between every service and machines are communicate with ports  


---

🧠 Simple Definition

A port is a number that identifies a specific service or application running on a computer.

Think of an IP address as a house, and ports as room numbers inside that house.

IP address = location of the device

Port number = which application you want to talk to inside that device



---

🔹 Why Ports Are Needed

Many services run on the same machine.
Ports help identify which service should receive the data.


---

📌 Common Port Numbers

Port	Service	Meaning

22	SSH	Remote login
80	HTTP	Websites (normal HTTP)
443	HTTPS	Secure websites
3306	MySQL	Database
5432	PostgreSQL	Database
25	SMTP	Email sending
53	DNS	Domain name system



---

🔹 Types of Ports

1. TCP Ports

Used for reliable communication
Example: SSH, HTTP, HTTPS

2. UDP Ports

Used for fast communication
Example: DNS, video streaming, games


---

🔹 Port Range

Range	       Name	                                  Use

0–1023	        Well-known ports	            Reserved for standard services
1024–49151	Registered ports	                 Used by apps
