# 🔹 Types of Network Media

## 1️⃣ Guided Media (Wired Media)

Data travels through a **physical cable**.

---

## 🧵 1. Twisted Pair Cable

Most commonly used network cable.

### Types:

### 🔹 a) UTP (Unshielded Twisted Pair)

* Cheap & flexible
* Used in LAN

**Examples:**

* Cat5 – 100 Mbps
* Cat5e – 1 Gbps
* Cat6 – 10 Gbps

📌 Used in: Offices, homes

---

### 🔹 b) STP (Shielded Twisted Pair)

* Extra shielding
* Less interference

📌 Used in: Industrial areas

---

## 📡 2. Coaxial Cable

* Single copper core
* Better noise resistance than twisted pair

**Examples:**

* Cable TV
* Old Ethernet (10Base2)

📌 Less used today

---

## 🔦 3. Fiber Optic Cable (FAST & LONG DISTANCE ⭐)

* Uses **light signals**
* Very high speed
* Immune to EMI

### Types:

🔹 **Single Mode Fiber (SMF)**

* Long distance (kms)
* Telecom, ISP

🔹 **Multi Mode Fiber (MMF)**

* Short distance
* Data centers

📌 Used in: Backbone networks, WAN

---

## 2️⃣ Unguided Media (Wireless Media)

Data travels through **air** (no cable).

---

## 📶 1. Radio Waves

* Omnidirectional
* Short to medium range

📌 Used in:

* Wi-Fi
* Bluetooth

---

## 📡 2. Microwaves

* Line-of-sight
* High frequency

📌 Used in:

* Mobile communication
* Satellite links

---

## 🌐 3. Infrared

* Very short range
* Line-of-sight

📌 Used in:

* TV remotes
* Old mobile data transfer

---

## 🛰️ 4. Satellite Communication

* Covers large areas
* High latency

📌 Used in:

* GPS
* TV broadcast
* Internet in remote areas

---

