# FLSM and VLSM (Subnetting Methods)

---

## 1️⃣ What is Subnetting? (Quick Recall)

Subnetting is the process of **dividing one network into smaller networks** to:

* Use IP addresses efficiently
* Improve management and security

---

## 2️⃣ FLSM (Fixed Length Subnet Mask) ⭐

### 2.1 What is FLSM?

**FLSM** means:

* All subnets use the **same subnet mask**
* All subnets have **equal number of hosts**

📌 One size fits all

---

### 2.2 Characteristics of FLSM ⭐

* Same mask for every subnet
* Same host capacity in all subnets
* Easy to design and understand
* Wastes IP addresses if host requirements differ

---

### 2.3 Example (Conceptual)

If you divide a network into 4 subnets using FLSM:

* Each subnet will have **equal size**
* Even small departments get large address space

---

### 2.4 When to Use FLSM?

* When all subnets need **same number of hosts**
* Small or simple networks
* Older/classful networks

---

## 3️⃣ VLSM (Variable Length Subnet Mask) ⭐⭐⭐

### 3.1 What is VLSM?

**VLSM** means:

* Different subnets use **different subnet masks**
* Each subnet is sized **based on actual host need**

📌 Right size for each subnet

---

### 3.2 Characteristics of VLSM ⭐

* Efficient IP address usage
* Different subnet sizes
* More complex than FLSM
* Requires planning

---

### 3.3 Example (Conceptual)

If a network has:

* Dept A: 100 hosts
* Dept B: 25 hosts
* Dept C: 10 hosts

With VLSM:

* Dept A gets large subnet
* Dept B gets medium subnet
* Dept C gets small subnet

No IP wastage ✅

---

## 4️⃣ Key Difference: FLSM vs VLSM ⭐⭐⭐

| Feature     | FLSM         | VLSM            |
| ----------- | ------------ | --------------- |
| Subnet size | Same for all | Different sizes |
| Subnet mask | Single       | Multiple        |
| IP usage    | Wastes IPs   | Efficient       |
| Complexity  | Simple       | Complex         |
| Flexibility | Low          | High            |

---

## 5️⃣ Important Rules to Remember ⭐

### FLSM Rule:

> Decide subnet count first → same mask everywhere

### VLSM Rule:

> Decide host requirement first → largest subnet first

---

## 6️⃣ Real-Life Analogy ⭐

| Concept | Analogy                      |
| ------- | ---------------------------- |
| FLSM    | Same size rooms for everyone |
| VLSM    | Rooms sized as per need      |

---

## 7️⃣ Interview One-Liners ⭐⭐⭐

* FLSM uses **fixed subnet mask**
* VLSM uses **variable subnet masks**
* VLSM reduces IP wastage
* FLSM is easier but inefficient
* VLSM is modern and widely used

---

## 8️⃣ One-Line Summary ⭐⭐⭐

> **FLSM divides networks into equal-sized subnets, while VLSM allows different-sized subnets based on host requirements.**
